    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d241">

                <pb facs="0435" n="303" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg303"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source"> Truman Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 241<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Acting
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<hi rendition="#small-caps">On Board
                            the</hi> U. S. S. “<placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Augusta</hi>
                        </placeName>”,] <lb/>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-12">12 July 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> MR–<hi rendition="#small-caps">in</hi>–35. Reference your MR-<hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">out</hi>-99 (State Department No. 16, 11
                        July).<anchor n="1" xml:id="d241-f1"/> I concur with your recommendation and
                    approve your suggested approach to the British Government.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
